drm/amdgpu: Add a new NPA Address space

jira KERNEL-1957
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-6.12.0-264.19.1.el10_3
commit-author Mukul Joshi <mukul.joshi@amd.com>
commit 09152b002ffde5bc769656aaa42728a2046c8bb5
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-6.12.0-264.19.1.el10_3/09152b00.failed

Add a new address space for NPA address management.
This is needed for sharing buffer objects across GPUs
with each running their own OS. The NPA address space
size can change across different HW generations so the
size is initialized during early init of the driver boot
up process.

	Signed-off-by: Mukul Joshi <mukul.joshi@amd.com>
	Reviewed-by: Felix Kuehling <felix.kuehling@amd.com>
	Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
(cherry picked from commit 09152b002ffde5bc769656aaa42728a2046c8bb5)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ualink.h
